# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_routes_coverage.py" "ROUTES COVERAGE GATE: PASS" "cross-tier route framework coverage (NestJS / ASP.NET / Ktor / Phoenix / Hapi / FastAPI-prefix)" "cross-tier ROUTE-DEFINITION coverage: MEASURE-FIRST found six common full-stack frameworks were silently missed (backend defined a route + frontend fetched it but no couple emerged). NestJS @Get(':id') is RELATIVE to @Controller('orders') -- the per-method route normalized to /{} (ubiquitous, dropped); ASP.NET [HttpGet('{id}')] is RELATIVE to [Route('api/orders')] and minimal-API app.MapGet had no .cs branch; Ktor get('/x') DSL was unmatched (.kt only saw Spring annotations); Phoenix get '/x' under scope '/api' was missed and .ex/.exs were not even in BACKEND_EXT; Hapi server.route({path}) was unmatched; FastAPI @router.get('/{id}') under APIRouter(prefix='/api/items') normalized to /{} because _PY_PREFIX was defined but never wired. Fix joins controller/router/scope prefixes to method routes (recall-biased: keeps method routes AS-IS plus each prefix-join). RECALL-SAFE + PRECISION-SAFE: the specificity floor + concrete-anchor matcher + multi-definer suppression are untouched, so a fabricated prefix-join can only fail to match, never false-couple. Proven on crafted repos: all six frameworks couple, ubiquitous /health still does NOT, a prefix-joined multi-definer is still suppressed (single-definer recall preserved), and a bare config path:/settings.get('...') is NOT swept; content-free path strings only" "cross-tier route coupling now recovers the client/server contract for NestJS, ASP.NET Core (attribute + minimal API), Ktor, Phoenix, Hapi, and FastAPI APIRouter-prefix nesting -- frameworks whose routes were previously invisible because the controller/router/scope prefix was never joined to the per-method route -- without weakening the specificity floor or the multi-definer precision guard" 16
